[SIZE=6][B]Raise Weapon: Aim at Yourself / 舉槍瞄準自己[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]English[/B][/SIZE]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cainiao524/HD2-Projectile-Collision-Filter/v0.3.0-preview.8/docs/assets/raise-weapon-aim-at-yourself-cover.png[/IMG]

[B]Turn Raise Weapon into a self-aim pose[/B]

This mod replaces the [B]Raise Weapon[/B] emote animation so your character points the weapon toward themselves while playing it. Equip that emote and activate it using your own emote binding.

[B]Known issue: playing this emote while sprinting and shooting can cause a softlock. If it happens, cancel sprinting or switch weapons. This existing issue remains listed and is not marked fixed.[/B]

[URL=https://ayakamods.com/mods/raise-weapon-aims-at-yourself.3946/]Original animation page and download[/URL] · [URL=https://ayakamods.com/mods/p-11-self-hit-healing-p-11-%E6%B2%BB%E7%99%82%E6%89%8B%E6%A7%8D%E8%87%AA%E7%99%82.4166/]Pair with Projectile Collision Filter / P-11 self-healing[/URL]

[B]What this package provides[/B]

[LIST]
[*]A replacement animation and aiming pose for the Raise Weapon emote.
[*]Your own key bindings remain in use; no particular default key is assumed.
[*]Arsenal manages enablement and disabling.
[*]The animation package does not modify projectile collision, healing amount, health or other damage effects, and does not make P-11 work on its owner by itself.
[/LIST]

An animation change does not establish self-hit collision. For healing, install a compatible projectile self-hit mod separately and land an actual fired P-11 dart on the character.

[B]Install and use[/B]

[LIST=1]
[*]Close the game and download the existing animation package from this page.
[*]Import the original package into Arsenal. If another mod replaces the same Raise Weapon animation, disable one of them to avoid competing replacements of the same resource.
[*]Enable this animation mod and redeploy.
[*]Launch the game and equip the [B]Raise Weapon[/B] emote.
[*]Activate it using your own emote controls. Avoid combining sprinting, shooting and the emote; if you become stuck, cancel sprinting or switch weapons.
[*]To disable it or change animation packages, close the game first, make the change in Arsenal and redeploy.
[/LIST]

If the animation has not changed, confirm that Raise Weapon is equipped, then check whether another mod overrides the same animation resource. Use the controls configured in your game; no fixed key is required.

[B]Pairing with P-11 self-hit healing[/B]

Recommended separate companion: [URL=https://ayakamods.com/mods/p-11-self-hit-healing-p-11-%E6%B2%BB%E7%99%82%E6%89%8B%E6%A7%8D%E8%87%AA%E7%99%82.4166/]Projectile Collision Filter / P-11 self-healing[/URL]. Start with its [B]僅治療手槍 — P-11 only[/B] choice.

Manage the two mods independently. This package supplies the emote pose; Projectile Collision Filter allows qualifying local P-11 darts to collide with their owner. Healing still requires an actual dart hit and the game's native logic, with manual aiming and firing retained. Follow the self-hit mod's own page for loader, game-version and installation requirements.

The companion is not bundled with this animation package. Teammate homing is also a separate mod; this package adds no target lock or automatic firing.

[B]Version, compatibility and known limits[/B]

[LIST]
[*]Author: [B]losa[/B]
[*]Original mod name: [B]Raise weapon aims at yourself[/B]
[*]Original animation version: [B]2026-09-18[/B]
[*]Page category: [B]Characters[/B]
[*]Existing attachment size: [B]328.9 KB[/B]; check the actual page download
[*]This page update: Chinese/English descriptions and a separate cover; original download and version retained
[/LIST]

This update changes the cover and operating instructions. The animation package is unchanged, and no new gameplay test was performed. The sprinting-plus-shooting emote softlock remains a known limitation.

There is no complete test matrix for every weapon pose, game version or multiplayer display. The same pose is not guaranteed for every weapon, nor is visibility of the replaced animation to other players. User comments are not treated as verification of those cases.

This is a community mod, unaffiliated with Arrowhead Game Studios. Use the original package on this page for the animation replacement; install the companion separately, following its compatibility requirements, when you want P-11 self-healing.

The current projectile mod and offline toolkit are on [URL=https://github.com/cainiao524/HD2-Projectile-Collision-Filter/releases/tag/v0.3.0-preview.8]GitHub Release[/URL]. The new cover uses blue fragments and a sci-fi character with the pistol held upright away from the helmet. It is promotional artwork, not a precise depiction of the in-game pose. This update changes copy and artwork only, not the animation package.

